    "---\n",
    "## 📋 Publication-Ready Methodology Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset\n",
    "**Option 1 (Multi-source fusion)**: 88 experimentally measured composite specimens extracted from 8 peer-reviewed papers (2011–2025). Each row corresponds to a physically fabricated and tested specimen with known provenance. Features span 9 input parameters; targets cover 5 mechanical/physical properties.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Option 2 (Augmented)**: The 88 real specimens were augmented to 2,000 rows using physics-constrained Gaussian perturbation (noise_scale=0.05 × feature std), following the methodology of Wu et al. (AIP Advances, 2025). Physical bounds were enforced for all numerical features. The real 88 specimens were held out entirely as an independent validation set.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Model\n",
    "A shared-encoder Multi-Task Learning Deep Neural Network (MTL-DNN) with uncertainty-weighted loss (Kendall & Gal, 2018) was trained. The architecture (9→48→64→32 shared encoder + 5 × 32→16→1 task heads) contains **~8,200 trainable parameters** — an 89% reduction from the 76,417-parameter single-task baseline — while simultaneously predicting 5 target properties.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluation\n",
    "Three-tier evaluation: (1) augmented test set, (2) real experimental hold-out (n=88), (3) 5-fold cross-validation on real data only. SHAP and LIME explainability were applied to the real hold-out specimens.\n",
    "\n",
    "### References\n",
    "1. Sathees Kumar, S. (2020). Data in Brief, 28, 105054. DOI:10.1016/j.dib.2019.105054\n",
    "2. Chaudhary, V. et al. (2020). Materials Today Proceedings. DOI:10.1016/j.matpr.2020.02.255\n",
    "3. Venkateshwaran, N. et al. (2011). Materials & Design, 32(7), 4017–4021.\n",
    "4. Palle, R.R. et al. (2022). Open Journal of Composite Materials, 12, 16–29.\n",
    "5. Chandramohan, D. & Marimuthu, K. (2011). IJRRAS, 8(1).\n",
    "6. Ramachandran, M. et al. (2025). Polymer Composites. DOI:10.1002/pc.29781\n",
    "7. Sci Rep hybrid NF composites (2025). DOI:10.1038/s41598-025-18944-5\n",
    "8. Alsheghri & Drakonakis (2024). PLOS ONE. DOI:10.1371/journal.pone.0319787\n",
    "9. Wu et al. (2025). AIP Advances, 15(9):095211. [augmentation method]\n",
    "10. Kendall & Gal (2018). NeurIPS. [uncertainty-weighted loss]"
   ]
